summary:
  The listener's own mute stands through anything that lifts the stream, so
  it is back at the next zero the widget writes by itself.

history:
  A device is told zero for the listener's mute and for nothing else: not
  for the zero a start, the end of a fade or a calibration writes. A start
  after a mute brings this computer's sound back by itself, and the mute
  ends there. Left standing, it reads as a mute again at the next
  calibration, and a touch of the device's row or a click on the slider
  then silences a television that nobody muted.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
      return stood === true && !(typeof level === "number" && level > 0);

replace:
      return stood === true;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_anything_that_lifts_the_stream_ends_the_mute
  and tests/qml/tst_volumeroad.qml::test_a_mute_that_a_start_lifted_is_not_back_at_the_next_zero.
  Line-neutral.
